IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Part IV of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory), the rules of reading: sections 18 to 38A.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- Section 17 (definitions) is in nt-part4-definitions.l4.
-- Sections 25(2) to (4), 28, 29 and 30 (service day, reckoning of time, 24 hour clock and age) are in nt-interpretation-time.l4.
-- Each rule is a function over a small typed description of what the rule operates on.
-- A function answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes or no (a "means" or "is" definition, an "if" or "where" condition, a flat negative),
-- and NOTHING where the text lists without closing the list, says "includes", leaves a term to another law, or does not speak to the case.

§ `Section 18: definitions read in context`

-- Definitions in or applicable to an Act apply except so far as the context or subject matter otherwise indicates or requires.
-- src:417 | Definitions in or applicable to an Act apply except so far as the context or subject matter otherwise indicates or requires.
@ref s 18 (src:417)
GIVEN `the context or subject matter indicates or requires that the definition does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18: a definition in or applicable to an Act applies` MEANS
    JUST (NOT `the context or subject matter indicates or requires that the definition does not apply`)

§ `Section 18A: Agencies`

-- An Agency is a department or unit of a department, or other authority or body, that is nominated as an Agency in an Administrative Arrangements Order or declared by an Act to be an Agency.
-- src:419 | (1) An Agency is a department or unit of a department, or other authority or body:
-- src:420 | (a) nominated as an Agency in an Administrative Arrangements Order; or
-- src:421 | (b) declared by an Act to be an Agency for the Public Sector Employment and Management Act 1993 or the Financial Management Act 1995.
@ref s 18A(1) (src:419-421)
GIVEN `it is a department or unit of a department, or other authority or body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is nominated as an Agency in an Administrative Arrangements Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Act declares it to be an Agency for the Public Sector Employment and Management Act 1993 or the Financial Management Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18A(1): the body is an Agency` MEANS
    JUST (`it is a department or unit of a department, or other authority or body`
          AND (`it is nominated as an Agency in an Administrative Arrangements Order`
               OR `an Act declares it to be an Agency for the Public Sector Employment and Management Act 1993 or the Financial Management Act 1995`))

-- A reference to the Agency in a provision is a reference to the Agency administering the provision.
-- src:422 | (2) A reference to the Agency in a provision of an Act is a reference to the Agency administering the provision in which the expression occurs.
@ref s 18A(2) (src:422)
GIVEN `the Agency administering the provision in which the expression occurs` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 18A(2): the Agency that "the Agency" refers to in a provision` MEANS `the Agency administering the provision in which the expression occurs`

-- A reference to the Agency administering a provision, or having responsibility for an area or activity, is a reference to the Agency to which an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act allocates it.
-- src:423 | (3) A reference to the Agency administering a provision of an Act or having responsibility for an area or activity of government is a reference to the Agency to which the administration of the provision or responsibility for the area or activity is allocated by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act.
@ref s 18A(3) (src:423)
GIVEN `the Agency to which an Administrative Arrangements Order allocates the administration or responsibility` IS A MAYBE STRING
      `the Agency to which an Act allocates the administration or responsibility` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`s 18A(3): the Agencies that the reference is a reference to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Agency to which an Administrative Arrangements Order allocates the administration or responsibility`
    WHEN JUST byOrder THEN
        CONSIDER `the Agency to which an Act allocates the administration or responsibility`
        WHEN JUST byAct THEN JUST (LIST byOrder, byAct)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (LIST byOrder)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the Agency to which an Act allocates the administration or responsibility`
        WHEN JUST byAct THEN JUST (LIST byAct)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- A reference to a specified Agency (including one that no longer exists) includes a reference to the department, authority or body to which the administration of the provision is allocated.
-- src:424 | (4) A reference to a specified Agency (including a reference to an Agency that no longer exists) in a provision of an Act includes a reference to the department, authority or body to which the administration of the provision is allocated by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act.
@ref s 18A(4) (src:424)
GIVEN `the specified Agency` IS A STRING
      `the department, authority or body to which the administration of the provision is allocated by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 18A(4): what a reference to the specified Agency includes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the department, authority or body to which the administration of the provision is allocated by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST `the specified Agency`
    WHEN JUST allocated THEN LIST `the specified Agency`, allocated

§ `Section 19: Ministerial references`

-- A minister is a person holding a Ministerial office.
-- src:426 | (1) A minister is a person holding a Ministerial office.
@ref s 19(1) (src:426)
GIVEN `the person holds a Ministerial office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(1): the person is a minister` MEANS JUST `the person holds a Ministerial office`

-- A reference to the Minister is a reference to the minister administering the Act (each of them, to the extent administering it in the relevant respect, where several administer it in different respects), and includes a minister acting for the Minister.
-- src:427 | (2) A reference in an Act to the Minister:
-- src:428 | (a) is a reference to:
-- src:429 | (i) the minister administering the Act in or for which the expression is used; or
-- src:430 | (ii) if different ministers are administering the Act in different respects, each of the ministers to the extent the minister is administering it in the relevant respect; and
-- src:431 | (b) includes a minister acting for the Minister.
@ref s 19(2) (src:427-431)
GIVEN `the person is a minister administering the Act in or for which the expression is used, in the relevant respect where different ministers administer it in different respects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a minister acting for the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(2): the person is referred to by "the Minister" in the Act` MEANS
    IF   `the person is a minister administering the Act in or for which the expression is used, in the relevant respect where different ministers administer it in different respects`
         OR `the person is a minister acting for the Minister`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- A reference to the minister administering a provision, or having responsibility for an area or activity, is a reference to the minister to whom it is allocated by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act.
-- src:432 | (3) A reference to the minister administering a provision of an Act or having responsibility for an area or activity of government is a reference to the minister to whom the provision or responsibility for the area or activity is allocated by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act.
@ref s 19(3) (src:432)
GIVEN `the minister to whom an Administrative Arrangements Order allocates the administration or responsibility` IS A MAYBE STRING
      `the minister to whom an Act allocates the administration or responsibility` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`s 19(3): the ministers that the reference is a reference to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the minister to whom an Administrative Arrangements Order allocates the administration or responsibility`
    WHEN JUST byOrder THEN
        CONSIDER `the minister to whom an Act allocates the administration or responsibility`
        WHEN JUST byAct THEN JUST (LIST byOrder, byAct)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (LIST byOrder)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the minister to whom an Act allocates the administration or responsibility`
        WHEN JUST byAct THEN JUST (LIST byAct)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- A reference to the Minister or a specified minister (including one that no longer exists) includes a reference to the minister to whom the administration of the provision is allocated.
-- src:433 | (4) A reference in a provision of an Act to the Minister or a specified minister (including a reference to a minister that no longer exists) includes a reference to the minister to whom the administration of the provision is allocated by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act.
@ref s 19(4) (src:433)
GIVEN `the specified minister` IS A STRING
      `the minister to whom the administration of the provision is allocated by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 19(4): what a reference to the specified minister includes` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the minister to whom the administration of the provision is allocated by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST `the specified minister`
    WHEN JUST allocated THEN LIST `the specified minister`, allocated

-- If a provision refers to the Minister and its administration has not been allocated to a minister, the reference is a reference to any minister.
-- src:434 | (5) If a reference is made in a provision of an Act to the Minister and the administration of the provision has not been allocated to a minister by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act, the reference is a reference to any minister.
@ref s 19(5) (src:434)
GIVEN `the provision refers to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the administration of the provision has been allocated to a minister by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19(5): the reference is a reference to any minister` MEANS
    JUST (`the provision refers to the Minister`
          AND (NOT `the administration of the provision has been allocated to a minister by an Administrative Arrangements Order or Act`))

§ `Section 19A: domestic relationships`

-- Spouse of a person means a person validly married to the person under the Marriage Act 1961 of the Commonwealth
-- or, if both are Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander, a person married to the person according to the customs and traditions of the community with which either identifies.
-- src:436 | (1) In any Act:
-- src:437 | spouse, of a person, means:
-- src:438 | (a) a person to whom the person is validly married under the Marriage Act 1961 of the Commonwealth; or
-- src:439 | (b) if the person is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander – an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander to whom the person is married according to the customs and traditions of the particular community of Aboriginals or Torres Strait Islanders with which either person identifies.
@ref s 19A(1) (src:436-439)
GIVEN `the two are validly married under the Marriage Act 1961 of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the two are married according to the customs and traditions of the particular community with which either identifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19A(1): the other person is a spouse of the person` MEANS
    JUST (`the two are validly married under the Marriage Act 1961 of the Commonwealth`
          OR (`the person is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander`
              AND `the other person is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander`
              AND `the two are married according to the customs and traditions of the particular community with which either identifies`))

-- Marriage, husband, wife, widow and widower have the meanings that correspond with the meaning of spouse.
-- src:440 | (2) In any Act, marriage, husband, wife, widow and widower have the meanings that correspond with the meaning of spouse.
@ref s 19A(2) (src:440)
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19A(2): the term has the meaning that corresponds with the meaning of spouse` MEANS
    IF   any (GIVEN known YIELD known EQUALS term) (LIST "marriage", "husband", "wife", "widow", "widower")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- De facto partner and de facto relationship have the meanings in section 3(1) of the De Facto Relationships Act (not among the sources).
-- src:441 | (3) In any Act, de facto partner and de facto relationship have the meanings in section 3(1) of the De Facto Relationships Act.
@ref s 19A(3) (src:441)
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 19A(3): where the meaning of the term is to be found` MEANS
    IF   any (GIVEN known YIELD known EQUALS term) (LIST "de facto partner", "de facto relationship")
    THEN JUST "section 3(1) of the De Facto Relationships Act"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Stepchild of a person is a child who, if the person is married, is a child of the person's spouse but not of the person,
-- or, if the person is in a de facto relationship, is a child of the person's de facto partner but not of the person.
-- src:442 | (4) In any Act:
-- src:443 | stepchild, of a person, means a child who is:
-- src:444 | (a) if the person is married – a child of the person's spouse but not a child of the person; or
-- src:445 | (b) if the person is in a de facto relationship – a child of the person's de facto partner but not a child of the person.
@ref s 19A(4) (src:442-445)
GIVEN `the person is married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in a de facto relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is a child of the person's spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is a child of the person's de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is a child of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19A(4): the child is a stepchild of the person` MEANS
    JUST ((NOT `the child is a child of the person`)
          AND ((`the person is married` AND `the child is a child of the person's spouse`)
               OR (`the person is in a de facto relationship` AND `the child is a child of the person's de facto partner`)))

-- A reference to a step-relative of a person has the meaning that corresponds with the meaning of stepchild.
-- src:446 | (5) In any Act, a reference to a step-relative of a person is read as having the meaning that corresponds with the meaning of stepchild.
@ref s 19A(5) (src:446)
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19A(5): the term has the meaning that corresponds with the meaning of stepchild` MEANS
    IF   term EQUALS "step-relative"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 20 to 23A: statutory instruments, "under an Act", amending Acts, grammatical forms and spelling`

-- Words, expressions and provisions in a statutory instrument have the same interpretation, application and effect as in the Act under which the instrument is made, granted or issued.
-- src:448 | (1) Words, expressions and provisions in a statutory instrument have the same interpretation, application and effect as they have in the Act under which the instrument is made, granted or issued.
@ref s 20(1) (src:448)
GIVEN `the meaning in the Act under which the instrument is made, granted or issued` IS A STRING
      `the word, expression or provision is in a statutory instrument made, granted or issued under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 20(1): the meaning that a word, expression or provision has in a statutory instrument` MEANS
    IF   `the word, expression or provision is in a statutory instrument made, granted or issued under that Act`
    THEN JUST `the meaning in the Act under which the instrument is made, granted or issued`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- A reference in a statutory instrument to the Act is a reference to the Act under which the instrument is made, granted or issued.
-- src:449 | (2) A reference in a statutory instrument to the Act is a reference to the Act under which the instrument is made, granted or issued.
@ref s 20(2) (src:449)
GIVEN `the Act under which the instrument is made, granted or issued` IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 20(2): the Act that "the Act" refers to in a statutory instrument` MEANS `the Act under which the instrument is made, granted or issued`

-- "By, under, pursuant to or in pursuance of" an Act means by, under, pursuant to or in pursuance of that Act or a statutory instrument under it.
-- src:451 | In an Act, by, under, pursuant to or in pursuance of that Act or another Act means by, under, pursuant to or in pursuance of that Act or other Act or a statutory instrument under that Act or other Act.
@ref s 21 (src:451)
GIVEN `it is by, under, pursuant to or in pursuance of the Act itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is by, under, pursuant to or in pursuance of a statutory instrument under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21: the thing is by, under, pursuant to or in pursuance of the Act` MEANS
    JUST (`it is by, under, pursuant to or in pursuance of the Act itself`
          OR `it is by, under, pursuant to or in pursuance of a statutory instrument under the Act`)

-- Words, expressions and provisions in an Act amending another Act have the same interpretation, application and effect as in the Act being amended.
-- src:453 | Words, expressions and provisions contained in an Act amending another Act shall have the same interpretation, application and effect as in that Act being amended.
@ref s 22 (src:453)
GIVEN `the meaning in the Act being amended` IS A STRING
      `the word, expression or provision is in an Act amending another Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 22: the meaning that a word, expression or provision has in an amending Act` MEANS
    IF   `the word, expression or provision is in an Act amending another Act`
    THEN JUST `the meaning in the Act being amended`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Where a word or phrase is given a particular meaning, its other parts of speech and grammatical forms have corresponding meanings.
-- src:455 | In an Act, where a word or phrase is given a particular meaning, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of that word or phrase have corresponding meanings.
@ref s 23 (src:455)
GIVEN `the word or phrase is given a particular meaning in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is another part of speech or grammatical form of that word or phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23: the form has a corresponding meaning` MEANS
    JUST (`the word or phrase is given a particular meaning in the Act` AND `the form is another part of speech or grammatical form of that word or phrase`)

-- Where a defined word's spelling no longer matches current drafting practice, subordinate legislation and other legislation may spell it in the current way, and the idea is not different merely because of the spelling.
-- src:457 | (1) This section applies to a word or term defined in a particular way in an Act if the spelling of the word, or a word in the term, is no longer consistent with current legislative drafting practice.
-- src:458 | (2) In subordinate legislation made under that Act or in other Acts or subordinate legislation, the word may be spelt in accordance with current legislative drafting practice and, if it is so spelt, the idea expressed must not be taken to be different merely because of the spelling.
@ref s 23A(1), (2) (src:457-458)
GIVEN `the word or term is defined in a particular way in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its spelling is no longer consistent with current legislative drafting practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is used in subordinate legislation made under that Act or in other Acts or subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is spelt in accordance with current legislative drafting practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23A: the idea is taken to be different because of the spelling` MEANS
    IF   `the word or term is defined in a particular way in an Act`
         AND `its spelling is no longer consistent with current legislative drafting practice`
         AND `it is used in subordinate legislation made under that Act or in other Acts or subordinate legislation`
         AND `it is spelt in accordance with current legislative drafting practice`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 24 to 24AA: gender, number, ranges and persons generally`

-- Language that indicates or could be taken to indicate a person of a particular gender or sex includes any individual, regardless of gender or sex.
-- src:462 | (1) In an Act, any language that indicates or could be taken to indicate a person of a particular gender or sex includes any individual, regardless of gender or sex.
@ref s 24(1) (src:462)
GIVEN `the language indicates or could be taken to indicate a person of a particular gender or sex` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(1): the language includes the individual, regardless of gender or sex` MEANS
    IF   `the language indicates or could be taken to indicate a person of a particular gender or sex` AND `the person is an individual`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Number of a word` IS ONE OF
    `singular`
    `plural`

-- Words in the singular include the plural, and words in the plural include the singular.
-- Example 1: the word "dog" includes the word "dogs".  Example 2: the word "cats" includes the word "cat".
-- src:463 | (2) In an Act:
-- src:464 | (a) words in the singular include the plural; and
-- src:465 | (b) words in the plural include the singular.
@ref s 24(2) (src:463-465)
GIVEN `the number of the word as used` IS A `Number of a word`
      `the word in the other number` IS A STRING
      `the word as used and the word in the other number are the singular and the plural of one word` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(2): the word as used includes the word in the other number` MEANS
    IF   `the word as used and the word in the other number are the singular and the plural of one word`
    THEN CONSIDER `the number of the word as used`
         WHEN `singular` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `plural` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The numbers, words or things that indicate the beginning and end of a range are included in the range.
-- Example 1: a reference to sections 56 to 60 includes sections 56 and 60.
-- src:470 | If an Act refers to a range of numbers, words or other things, the numbers, words or things indicating the beginning and end of the range are included in the range.
@ref s 24A (src:470)
GIVEN `the number that indicates the beginning of the range` IS A NUMBER
      `the number that indicates the end of the range` IS A NUMBER
      `the number asked about` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24A: the number is included in the range of numbers` MEANS
    IF   `the number that indicates the beginning of the range` AT MOST `the number asked about`
         AND `the number asked about` AT MOST `the number that indicates the end of the range`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Example 2: a reference to all the words from eagle to kite includes eagle and kite.
-- Words are put in order as a dictionary puts them.
@ref s 24A (src:470)
GIVEN `the word that indicates the beginning of the range` IS A STRING
      `the word that indicates the end of the range` IS A STRING
      `the word asked about` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24A: the word is included in the range of words` MEANS
    IF   `the word that indicates the beginning of the range` AT MOST `the word asked about`
         AND `the word asked about` AT MOST `the word that indicates the end of the range`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body politic`
    `a body corporate`
    `something that is none of these`

-- A reference in an Act to a person generally includes a body politic and a body corporate as well as an individual.
-- Examples: anyone, no-one, party, someone.
-- src:475 | (1) In an Act, a reference to a person generally includes a reference to a body politic and body corporate as well as an individual.
@ref s 24AA(1) (src:475)
GIVEN `the reference is to a person generally` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24AA(1): the reference to a person generally includes the kind of person` MEANS
    IF   `the reference is to a person generally`
    THEN CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `something that is none of these` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (1) is not displaced merely because elsewhere in the Act there is an express reference to an individual, a body politic or a body corporate.
-- src:481 | (2) Subsection (1) is not displaced merely because there is an express reference to either an individual, body politic or body corporate elsewhere in the Act.
@ref s 24AA(2) (src:481)
GIVEN `the only reason offered is that elsewhere in the Act there is an express reference to either an individual, a body politic or a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24AA(2): subsection (1) is displaced` MEANS
    IF   `the only reason offered is that elsewhere in the Act there is an express reference to either an individual, a body politic or a body corporate`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 25: service of documents`

DECLARE `Kind of recipient` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body`

DECLARE `Person to whom a document is given` IS ONE OF
    `the recipient`
    `an executive officer of the body`
    `a person authorised by the recipient to receive the document`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Way of serving a document under section 25(1)` IS ONE OF
    `giving it to a person`
        HAS `the person to whom it is given` IS A `Person to whom a document is given`
    `sending it by prepaid post addressed to the recipient at the recipient's address`
    `sending it to the recipient by fax`
    `leaving it, addressed to the recipient, at the recipient's address with someone`
        HAS `the person appears to be at least 16 years old` IS A BOOLEAN
            `the person appears to live or be employed there` IS A BOOLEAN

-- A person may serve a document on an individual or a body by giving it to the recipient (an individual), to an executive officer (a body) or to a person the recipient authorises,
-- by prepaid post to the recipient's address, by fax, or by leaving it at the recipient's address with someone who appears to be at least 16 and to live or be employed there.
-- A way the paragraphs do not list is not said to be allowed or barred.
-- src:483 | (1) A person may serve a document on an individual or body (the recipient):
-- src:484 | (a) by giving it to:
-- src:485 | (i) if the recipient is an individual – the recipient; or
-- src:486 | (ii) if the recipient is a body – an executive officer of the body; or
-- src:487 | (iii) in any case – a person authorised by the recipient to receive the document; or
-- src:488 | (b) by sending it by prepaid post addressed to the recipient at the recipient's address; or
-- src:489 | (c) by sending it to the recipient by fax; or
-- src:490 | (d) by leaving it, addressed to the recipient, at the recipient's address with someone who appears to be at least 16 years old and appears to live or be employed there.
@ref s 25(1) (src:483-490)
GIVEN recipient IS A `Kind of recipient`
      way IS A `Way of serving a document under section 25(1)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(1): a person may serve the document on the recipient in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `giving it to a person` whom THEN
        CONSIDER whom
        WHEN `the recipient` THEN IF recipient EQUALS `an individual` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `an executive officer of the body` THEN IF recipient EQUALS `a body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `a person authorised by the recipient to receive the document` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `sending it by prepaid post addressed to the recipient at the recipient's address` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sending it to the recipient by fax` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `leaving it, addressed to the recipient, at the recipient's address with someone` old live THEN
        IF   old AND live
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

-- The section has effect for the service of a document whether or not the word "serve" is used in the law providing for its service.
-- src:494 | (5) This section has effect for the service of a document whether or not the word serve is used in the law providing for the service of the document.
@ref s 25(5) (src:494)
GIVEN `the law provides for the service of the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word serve is used in that law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(5): section 25 has effect for the service of the document` MEANS
    IF   `the law provides for the service of the document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The address of a recipient includes the latest home and business addresses of the recipient that are recorded for a law in force in the Territory.
-- src:496 | address, of a recipient, includes the latest home and business addresses of the recipient that are recorded for a law in force in the Territory.
@ref s 25(6) "address" (src:496)
GIVEN `it is a latest home or business address of the recipient recorded for a law in force in the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(6) "address": the address is within the address of a recipient` MEANS
    IF `it is a latest home or business address of the recipient recorded for a law in force in the Territory` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- A body includes an incorporated body.
-- src:497 | body includes an incorporated body.
@ref s 25(6) "body" (src:497)
GIVEN `the body is an incorporated body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(6) "body": the body is within a body` MEANS
    IF `the body is an incorporated body` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- A document includes a notice and any other thing that may be sent by a method mentioned in subsection (1).
-- src:498 | document includes a notice and any other thing that may be sent by a method mentioned in subsection (1).
@ref s 25(6) "document" (src:498)
GIVEN `it is a notice or another thing that may be sent by a method mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(6) "document": the thing is within a document` MEANS
    IF `it is a notice or another thing that may be sent by a method mentioned in subsection (1)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- An executive officer of a body is, for an Agency, the Chief Executive Officer of the Agency, and otherwise a person (however described) concerned with, or participating in, the body's management.
-- src:499 | executive officer, of a body, means:
-- src:500 | (a) for an Agency – the Chief Executive Officer of the Agency. or
-- src:501 | (b) otherwise – a person (however described) who is concerned with, or participates in, the body's management.
@ref s 25(6) "executive officer" (src:499-501)
GIVEN `the body is an Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Chief Executive Officer of the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is concerned with, or participates in, the body's management` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(6) "executive officer": the person is an executive officer of the body` MEANS
    IF   `the body is an Agency`
    THEN JUST `the person is the Chief Executive Officer of the Agency`
    ELSE JUST `the person is concerned with, or participates in, the body's management`

§ `Sections 26 and 27: writing and distance`

-- References to writing include any mode of representing or reproducing words, figures or symbols in a visible form,
-- whether or not an optical, electronic, mechanical or other means or process must be used before they can be perceived.
-- src:503 | In an Act, words, expressions and provisions referring to writing shall be construed as including references to any mode of representing or reproducing words, figures or symbols in a visible form whether or not an optical, electronic, mechanical or other means or process must be used before they can be perceived.
@ref s 26 (src:503)
GIVEN `the mode represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a visible form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 26: the mode of representing or reproducing is within a reference to writing` MEANS
    IF   `the mode represents or reproduces words, figures or symbols` AND `it is in a visible form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Point in space` HAS
    `distance east in metres`  IS A NUMBER
    `distance north in metres` IS A NUMBER
    `height in metres`         IS A NUMBER

-- In the measurement of a distance for the purposes of an Act, the measurement is made in a straight line in a horizontal plane.
-- So the height of the two points is left out and the distance is that between the points as they lie on the horizontal plane.
-- src:505 | In the measurement of a distance for the purposes of an Act the measurement shall be made in a straight line in a horizontal plane.
@ref s 27 (src:505)
GIVEN from IS A `Point in space`
      to IS A `Point in space`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 27: the distance in metres between the two points measured in a straight line in a horizontal plane` MEANS
    SQRT (((to's `distance east in metres`) MINUS (from's `distance east in metres`)) TIMES ((to's `distance east in metres`) MINUS (from's `distance east in metres`))
          PLUS ((to's `distance north in metres`) MINUS (from's `distance north in metres`)) TIMES ((to's `distance north in metres`) MINUS (from's `distance north in metres`)))

§ `Section 31: the Sovereign`

-- A reference in an Act to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act, or to the Crown, is a reference to the Sovereign reigning for the time being.
-- src:521 | A reference in an Act to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act, or to the Crown, is a reference to the Sovereign reigning for the time being.
@ref s 31 (src:521)
GIVEN `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act, or to the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Sovereign reigning for the time being` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 31: the Sovereign to whom the reference is a reference` MEANS
    IF   `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act, or to the Crown`
    THEN JUST `the Sovereign reigning for the time being`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 34 and 34A: the Administrator and the Executive Council`

-- A power or function conferred on the Administrator is not to be read as exercisable except with the advice of the Executive Council,
-- save that the Administrator may act without it to fix a date for bringing an Act or subordinate legislation into operation,
-- for any other power or function the Administrator, with that advice, has determined by notice in the Gazette may be exercised without it,
-- and for powers and functions relating only to matters in respect of which the Ministers of the Territory have no executive authority.
-- src:523 | (1) Subject to this section, a provision of an Act that confers upon the Administrator a power or function shall not be read as requiring, permitting or enabling the Administrator to exercise that power or perform that function except with the advice of the Executive Council.
-- src:524 | (2) The Administrator may, without reference to the Executive Council:
-- src:525 | (a) exercise a power to fix a date for the bringing into operation of an Act or subordinate legislation or provisions of an Act or subordinate legislation; or
-- src:526 | (b) exercise any other power or perform any function that the Administrator, with the advice of the Executive Council, determines, by notice in the Gazette, to be a power that may be exercised, or a function that may be performed, as the case may be, by the Administrator without reference to the Executive Council.
-- src:527 | (3) The Administrator may, without reference to the Executive Council:
-- src:528 | (a) exercise any power where the exercise of that power relates only to; or
-- src:529 | (b) perform any function where the performance of that function relates only to,
-- src:530 | matters in respect of which the Ministers of the Territory do not have executive authority under section 35 of the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 34(1), (2), (3) (src:523-530)
GIVEN `the power is a power to fix a date for the bringing into operation of an Act or subordinate legislation or provisions of an Act or subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Administrator, with the advice of the Executive Council, has determined by notice in the Gazette that the power or function may be exercised or performed without reference to the Executive Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exercise of the power or performance of the function relates only to matters in respect of which the Ministers of the Territory do not have executive authority under section 35 of the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34: the Administrator may exercise the power or perform the function without the advice of the Executive Council` MEANS
    JUST (`the power is a power to fix a date for the bringing into operation of an Act or subordinate legislation or provisions of an Act or subordinate legislation`
          OR `the Administrator, with the advice of the Executive Council, has determined by notice in the Gazette that the power or function may be exercised or performed without reference to the Executive Council`
          OR `the exercise of the power or performance of the function relates only to matters in respect of which the Ministers of the Territory do not have executive authority under section 35 of the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 of the Commonwealth`)

-- A reference in an Act to the Administrator in Council is read as a reference to the Administrator, and section 34 applies accordingly.
-- src:532 | A reference in an Act to the Administrator in Council shall be read as a reference to the Administrator, and section 34 applies accordingly.
@ref s 34A (src:532)
GIVEN `the reference is a reference in an Act to the Administrator in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 34A: the reference is read as a reference to the Administrator, with section 34 applying` MEANS
    IF `the reference is a reference in an Act to the Administrator in Council` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 35 to 37: Administrative Arrangements Orders`

-- The Administrator may make an Administrative Arrangements Order.
-- The section does not say that no one else may.
-- src:534 | (1) The Administrator may make an Administrative Arrangements Order.
@ref s 35(1) (src:534)
GIVEN `the person is the Administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(1): the person may make an Administrative Arrangements Order` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Administrator` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Thing an Administrative Arrangements Order may do` IS ONE OF
    `nominate a department or other authority or body as an Agency`
    `allocate to a minister the administration of an Act or a provision of an Act`
    `allocate to a minister the responsibility for an area or activity of government or a government authority or government entity`
    `allocate to a minister the responsibility for an Agency nominated under paragraph (a)`
    `allocate to an Agency the administration of an Act or a provision of an Act`
    `allocate to an Agency the responsibility for an area or activity of government or a government authority or government entity`
    `some other thing`

-- An Administrative Arrangements Order may do any of the listed things.
-- The list is not closed with "only".
-- src:535 | (2) An Administrative Arrangements Order may do any of the following:
-- src:536 | (a) nominate a department or other authority or body as an Agency;
-- src:537 | (b) allocate to a specified minister or the minister holding a specified Ministerial office:
-- src:538 | (i) the administration of an Act or a provision of an Act; or
-- src:539 | (ii) the responsibility for an area or activity of government or a government authority or government entity; or
-- src:540 | (iii) responsibility for an Agency nominated under paragraph (a);
-- src:541 | (c) allocate to an Agency nominated under paragraph (a):
-- src:542 | (i) the administration of an Act or a provision of an Act; or
-- src:543 | (ii) the responsibility for an area or activity of government or a government authority or government entity.
@ref s 35(2) (src:535-543)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing an Administrative Arrangements Order may do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(2): an Administrative Arrangements Order may do the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `some other thing` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Arrangement for the administration of an Act` IS ONE OF
    `different provisions of an Act administered by different ministers`
    `different ministers administering an Act in different respects`
    `two or more ministers jointly administering the same Act or the same provisions of an Act`
    `some other arrangement`

-- For an allocation to a minister of the administration of an Act or provision, the three arrangements listed are available.
-- src:546 | (3) For subsection (2)(b)(i):
-- src:547 | (a) different provisions of an Act may be administered by different ministers; and
-- src:548 | (b) different ministers may administer an Act in different respects; and
-- src:549 | (c) 2 or more ministers may jointly administer the same Act or the same provisions of an Act.
@ref s 35(3) (src:546-549)
GIVEN arrangement IS A `Arrangement for the administration of an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(3): the arrangement is available for the administration of an Act or a provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER arrangement
    WHEN `some other arrangement` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The joint administration of an Act or provisions does not require the ministerial function to be exercised jointly.
-- src:550 | (4) For subsection (3)(c), the joint administration of an Act or provisions of an Act does not require the ministerial function to be exercised jointly.
@ref s 35(4) (src:550)
GIVEN `the Act or provisions are jointly administered by two or more ministers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(4): the joint administration requires the ministerial function to be exercised jointly` MEANS
    IF `the Act or provisions are jointly administered by two or more ministers` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Who administers an Act that no order allocates` HAS
    `the minister` IS A STRING
    `the Agency`   IS A STRING

-- The administration of an Act not allocated to a minister or an Agency by an Administrative Arrangements Order is allocated to the minister who has, and the Agency that has,
-- the responsibility for the area or activity to which the subject matter of the Act most closely relates under the order.
-- src:551 | (5) The administration of any Act not allocated to a minister or an Agency by an Administrative Arrangements Order is allocated to the minister who has, and the Agency that has, responsibility for the area or activity of government under the Administrative Arrangements Order to which the subject matter of the Act most closely relates.
@ref s 35(5) (src:551)
GIVEN `the administration of the Act is allocated to a minister or an Agency by an Administrative Arrangements Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minister with responsibility for the area or activity of government to which the subject matter of the Act most closely relates` IS A STRING
      `the Agency with responsibility for the area or activity of government to which the subject matter of the Act most closely relates` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Who administers an Act that no order allocates`)
`s 35(5): the minister and Agency to which the administration of the Act is allocated` MEANS
    IF   `the administration of the Act is allocated to a minister or an Agency by an Administrative Arrangements Order`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`Who administers an Act that no order allocates`
               WITH `the minister` IS `the minister with responsibility for the area or activity of government to which the subject matter of the Act most closely relates`,
                    `the Agency` IS `the Agency with responsibility for the area or activity of government to which the subject matter of the Act most closely relates`)

-- Notice of the making of an Administrative Arrangements Order must be published in the Gazette, and must specify where a copy may be obtained.
-- src:553 | (1) Notice of the making of an Administrative Arrangements Order must be published in the Gazette.
-- src:554 | (2) The notice must specify where a copy of the Administrative Arrangements Order may be obtained.
@ref s 36(1), (2) (src:553-554)
GIVEN `notice of the making of the order has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies where a copy of the order may be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 36(1), (2): the notice meets the requirements for an Administrative Arrangements Order` MEANS
    JUST (`notice of the making of the order has been published in the Gazette` AND `the notice specifies where a copy of the order may be obtained`)

-- An Administrative Arrangements Order takes effect when notice of its making is published, or at a later time specified in the order.
-- src:555 | (3) An Administrative Arrangements Order takes effect:
-- src:556 | (a) when notice of its making is published under subsection (1); or
-- src:557 | (b) at a later time specified in the Administrative Arrangements Order.
@ref s 36(3) (src:555-557)
GIVEN `the day on which notice of the making of the order is published` IS A DATE
      `the later day specified in the order, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 36(3): the day on which an Administrative Arrangements Order takes effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the later day specified in the order, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `the day on which notice of the making of the order is published`
    WHEN JUST later THEN
        IF   Day later GREATER THAN Day `the day on which notice of the making of the order is published`
        THEN JUST later
        ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Reference in an agreement` IS ONE OF
    `a reference to the Minister administering the first-mentioned Agency`
    `a reference to the first-mentioned Agency`

-- Where a Territory agreement refers to an Agency whose functions are afterwards allocated to another Agency, the reference to that Agency is read as a reference to the second Agency,
-- and the reference to the Minister administering the first Agency is read as a reference to the Minister administering the second, or a minister acting for the time being for that Minister.
-- src:559 | Where an agreement is entered into by or on behalf of the Territory and, after the date of the agreement, the functions of an Agency in relation to the administration of matters to which the agreement relates are or have been allocated to another Agency by an Administrative Arrangements Order or an Act:
-- src:560 | (a) a reference in the agreement to the Minister administering the first-mentioned Agency shall be read as a reference to the Minister administering the second-mentioned Agency or to a minister acting for the time being for him and on his behalf; and
-- src:561 | (b) a reference in the agreement to the first-mentioned Agency shall be read as a reference to the second-mentioned Agency.
@ref s 37 (src:559-561)
GIVEN reference IS A `Reference in an agreement`
      `the agreement is entered into by or on behalf of the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `after the date of the agreement the functions of the Agency in relation to the matters to which the agreement relates are or have been allocated to another Agency by an Administrative Arrangements Order or an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second-mentioned Agency` IS A STRING
      `the Minister administering the second-mentioned Agency` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 37: what the reference in the agreement is read as` MEANS
    IF   `the agreement is entered into by or on behalf of the Territory`
         AND `after the date of the agreement the functions of the Agency in relation to the matters to which the agreement relates are or have been allocated to another Agency by an Administrative Arrangements Order or an Act`
    THEN CONSIDER reference
         WHEN `a reference to the Minister administering the first-mentioned Agency` THEN JUST `the Minister administering the second-mentioned Agency`
         WHEN `a reference to the first-mentioned Agency` THEN JUST `the second-mentioned Agency`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 38 and 38A: offices, jurisdictions and Commonwealth references`

DECLARE `Thing referred to in section 38(1)` IS ONE OF
    `an officer or an office`
    `a locality, a jurisdiction or another matter or thing`
    `something other than an officer, office, locality or jurisdiction`

-- In an Act a reference to an officer or office is a reference to such an officer or office for the Territory,
-- and references to localities, jurisdictions and other matters and things are references to such localities, jurisdictions and matters and things in and of the Territory.
-- src:563 | (1) In an Act:
-- src:564 | (a) a reference to an officer or office shall be construed as a reference to such an officer or office for the Territory; and
-- src:565 | (b) references to localities, jurisdictions and other matters and things shall be construed as references to such localities, jurisdictions and other matters and things in and of the Territory.
@ref s 38(1) (src:563-565)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing referred to in section 38(1)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(1): the reference is construed as a reference to the thing for, or in and of, the Territory` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `something other than an officer, office, locality or jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Candidate for inclusion in a reference under section 38(2)` IS ONE OF
    `a person, officer, office or body for the time being having the power or function`
    `a person, officer, office or body specified by order of the Minister`
    `the Administrator`

-- Where the person, officer, office or body referred to no longer exists, or the power or function is no longer theirs, the reference is read as including, in order,
-- (a) whoever for the time being has the power or function, (b) failing that, whoever the Minister specifies by order, (c) failing both and with no minister or department administering the provision, the Administrator.
-- src:566 | (2) Where, in relation to a power or function, there is, in a provision of an Act or in an agreement entered into by or on behalf of the Territory, reference to a person, an officer, an office, a body corporate or a body of persons and there is no longer such a person, officer, office or body, or that power or function is no longer a power or function of that person, officer, office or body, the reference shall be read as including:
-- src:567 | (a) a reference to a person, officer, office or body for the time being having that power or function; or
-- src:568 | (b) if there is no person, officer, office or body for the time being having that power or function, a reference to such person, officer, office or body as is specified by order of the Minister administering that provision or administering the Department or other Agency the functions of which include the administration of matters to which the provision relates; or
-- src:569 | (c) if there is no person, officer, office or body for the time being having that power or function, no minister administering that provision and no department or other Agency with functions that include the administration of matters to which the provision relates, the Administrator.
@ref s 38(2) (src:566-569)
GIVEN candidate IS A `Candidate for inclusion in a reference under section 38(2)`
      `there is no longer such a person, officer, office or body, or the power or function is no longer theirs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a person, officer, office or body for the time being having the power or function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has specified a person, officer, office or body by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no minister administering the provision and no department or other Agency with functions that include the administration of matters to which the provision relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(2): the reference is read as including the candidate` MEANS
    JUST (`there is no longer such a person, officer, office or body, or the power or function is no longer theirs`
          AND (CONSIDER candidate
               WHEN `a person, officer, office or body for the time being having the power or function` THEN `there is a person, officer, office or body for the time being having the power or function`
               WHEN `a person, officer, office or body specified by order of the Minister` THEN
                    (NOT `there is a person, officer, office or body for the time being having the power or function`) AND `the Minister has specified a person, officer, office or body by order`
               WHEN `the Administrator` THEN
                    (NOT `there is a person, officer, office or body for the time being having the power or function`)
                    AND `there is no minister administering the provision and no department or other Agency with functions that include the administration of matters to which the provision relates`))

-- Where a person holding a particular designation, office or position is mentioned in general terms, the mention is read as including everyone who for the time being holds, occupies or performs the duties of it.
-- src:570 | (3) Where in an Act or in an order made under subsection (2), a person holding or occupying a particular designation, office or position is mentioned or referred to in general terms, the mention or reference shall be read as including a reference to all persons who at any time for the time being hold or occupy or perform the duties of that designation, office or position.
@ref s 38(3) (src:570)
GIVEN `a person holding or occupying a particular designation, office or position is mentioned in general terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds or occupies, or performs the duties of, that designation, office or position for the time being` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38(3): the mention includes the person` MEANS
    IF   `a person holding or occupying a particular designation, office or position is mentioned in general terms`
         AND `the person holds or occupies, or performs the duties of, that designation, office or position for the time being`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Notwithstanding section 38, a reference to a Commonwealth minister, department, office, officer, body corporate or body of persons is read as or as including whichever, Commonwealth or Territory, the Administrator determines by notice in the Gazette.
-- src:572 | (1) Notwithstanding section 38, where in a provision of an Act reference is made to a Commonwealth minister or department or to an office, officer, body corporate or body of persons established by or under an Act of the Commonwealth, that reference shall be read as or as including a reference to such minister, department, office, officer or body, whether Commonwealth or Territory, as is determined by the Administrator by notice published in the Gazette.
@ref s 38A(1) (src:572)
GIVEN `the reference is to a Commonwealth minister or department, or to an office, officer, body corporate or body of persons established by or under an Act of the Commonwealth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minister, department, office, officer or body determined by the Administrator by notice published in the Gazette` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 38A(1): what the reference to the Commonwealth minister, department or body is read as` MEANS
    IF   `the reference is to a Commonwealth minister or department, or to an office, officer, body corporate or body of persons established by or under an Act of the Commonwealth`
    THEN `the minister, department, office, officer or body determined by the Administrator by notice published in the Gazette`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Where a Commonwealth minister or department no longer exists and the Administrator has made no determination, the reference is read as a reference to the minister administering the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 of the Commonwealth, or that minister's department.
-- src:573 | (2) Where in a provision of an Act reference is made to a Commonwealth minister or department and there is no longer any such minister or department and no determination has been made under subsection (1), that reference shall be read as a reference to the minister for the time being administering the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 of the Commonwealth, or to the department of that minister, as the case may be.
@ref s 38A(2) (src:573)
GIVEN `the reference is to a Commonwealth minister or department` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no longer any such minister or department` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a determination has been made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 38A(2): the reference is read as a reference to the minister administering the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 of the Commonwealth, or to that minister's department` MEANS
    JUST (`the reference is to a Commonwealth minister or department`
          AND `there is no longer any such minister or department`
          AND (NOT `a determination has been made under subsection (1)`))
